WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.484 --> 00:00:08.520 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Welcome to Africa episode four of eight. First, I clear the chosen names for a
fresh regional lesson.

2
00:00:09.185 --> 00:00:21.294 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Eight countries connect desert Chad with the Congo forests and Atlantic
islands. São Tomé and Príncipe needs a labelled supplemental view because it
is absent from GeoClick’s native map.

3
00:00:22.145 --> 00:00:25.384 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Chad and its neighbours into view.

4
00:00:35.163 --> 00:00:46.332 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Chad is landlocked below Libya, east of Niger and west of Sudan. Cameroon and
the Central African Republic lie toward its south.

5
00:00:46.995 --> 00:00:58.210 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The lakes of Ounianga survive in a very dry Saharan landscape because
groundwater feeds them. Some lakes are fresh and others salty, despite lying
in the same desert region.

6
00:00:58.865 --> 00:01:08.675 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Picture surprising lakes in the desert above the Congo Basin. Chad is the tall
inland link between Libya and the Central African Republic.

7
00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:24.587 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Cameroon lies southeast of Nigeria, with Chad toward its northeast and Gabon,
Equatorial Guinea and the Republic of the Congo below. A southwestern coast
reaches the Gulf of Guinea.

8
00:01:25.252 --> 00:01:37.454 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The Dja Faunal Reserve is almost encircled by the Dja River. Its forest
supports many primates, with the river providing a remarkable natural
boundary.

9
00:01:38.112 --> 00:01:48.178 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember a river loop around rainforest. Cameroon is the coastal hinge between
West and Central Africa, below Nigeria’s eastern side.

10
00:01:51.966 --> 00:02:01.521 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The Central African Republic is landlocked below Chad and west of South Sudan.
Cameroon lies west, with the two Congos toward its south.

11
00:02:02.173 --> 00:02:15.559 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The Sangha Trinational landscape joins protected forests in the Central
African Republic, Cameroon and the Republic of the Congo. Forest clearings
provide gathering places for elephants and other animals.

12
00:02:16.223 --> 00:02:28.634 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Picture elephants in a forest clearing at a three-country meeting. The Central
African Republic sits inland above the Congo countries; its name describes its
broad position.

13
00:02:29.325 --> 00:02:32.994 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Equatorial Guinea and its neighbours into view.

14
00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:46.206 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Equatorial Guinea includes a small mainland part below Cameroon, plus islands
in the Gulf of Guinea. Bioko lies offshore; Gabon surrounds much of the
mainland part.

15
00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:58.760 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
This country’s geography is split between mainland and islands. Its name can
mislead: the mainland is north of the equator, while the island of Annobón
lies south of it.

16
00:02:59.418 --> 00:03:11.272 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember one country in separated pieces beside Cameroon and Gabon. Do not
confuse Equatorial Guinea with Guinea or Guinea-Bissau on the West African
coast.

17
00:03:11.956 --> 00:03:15.497 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Gabon and its neighbours into view.

18
00:03:17.975 --> 00:03:27.228 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Gabon faces the Atlantic below Equatorial Guinea and Cameroon. The Republic of
the Congo curves around its eastern and southern sides.

19
00:03:27.885 --> 00:03:40.424 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
At Lopé-Okanda, rainforest meets older savannah patches. The landscape also
preserves rock carvings and evidence of people moving through the Ogooué
valley over long periods.

20
00:03:41.079 --> 00:03:51.017 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Picture forest beside savannah on the equatorial Atlantic coast. Gabon is west
of the Republic of the Congo, with Equatorial Guinea tucked above it.

21
00:03:51.707 --> 00:03:55.887 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Republic of the Congo and its neighbours into view.

22
00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:10.155 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The Republic of the Congo lies east of Gabon and west of the much larger
Democratic Republic of the Congo. Its short southwestern coastline reaches the
Atlantic.

23
00:04:10.819 --> 00:04:24.078 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The Sangha forest landscape is shared with Cameroon and the Central African
Republic. It connects protected habitats for forest elephants, gorillas and
chimpanzees across national boundaries.

24
00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:38.347 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Congo-Brazzaville as the smaller western Congo. Its neighbour across
the great river is the Democratic Republic of the Congo; the similar names
identify separate countries.

25
00:04:40.712 --> 00:04:53.553 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The Democratic Republic of the Congo occupies a vast central area east of the
Republic of the Congo. It extends toward the Great Lakes in the east and has a
very short Atlantic outlet.

26
00:04:54.209 --> 00:05:05.807 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Virunga National Park contains an extraordinary range of habitats, from
volcanic landscapes to high mountains. Mountain gorillas live within this
diverse eastern border region.

27
00:05:06.465 --> 00:05:17.471 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Picture a huge central basin reaching east to volcanoes and gorillas. This is
Congo-Kinshasa, the larger Congo, not its smaller western neighbour.

28
00:05:18.832 --> 00:05:25.995 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's locate São Tomé and Príncipe on a labelled supplemental map, then move
in for a closer view.

29
00:05:30.033 --> 00:05:41.759 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
São Tomé and Príncipe is an Atlantic island country west of Gabon. Its two
main islands lie in the Gulf of Guinea, separate from mainland Central Africa.

30
00:05:42.415 --> 00:05:55.801 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
UNESCO’s Príncipe Biosphere Reserve recognises an island environment with
distinctive forest and marine habitats. Isolation helps explain why island
wildlife can differ from mainland wildlife.

31
00:05:56.456 --> 00:06:08.310 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember two islands off Gabon, not an extra mainland strip. Príncipe lies
northeast of São Tomé; this labelled supplemental view keeps their real
geographic positions.

32
00:06:14.119 --> 00:06:29.959 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Chad is above the Central African Republic. Cameroon reaches the Gulf of
Guinea; Equatorial Guinea and Gabon follow the coast south. The smaller
Republic of the Congo lies west of the much larger Democratic Republic of the
Congo.

33
00:06:30.618 --> 00:06:48.654 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Recall desert lakes, a river-ringed forest, elephant clearings, mainland and
island pieces, forest beside savannah and eastern volcanoes. São Tomé and
Príncipe is offshore west of Gabon, not on the mainland.
